  "notes": "Measured on the E175 N624UX (left, Aug 2026), checked on N609UX (2019) and the CRJ200 N463SW (2026). On the regional jets the title is much smaller than the mainline's and sits above the windows. Small black lettering by the forward door ('Operated by SkyWest', 'Connecting people. Uniting the world.') is too small to draw and changes with the operator. Many United Express jets still wear the 2010 scheme: see express-2010. Positions are measured on E175s, whose window line is higher (y about 0.3) than the narrow-body average in COORDINATES.md, so titles placed above or below the windows sit higher than they would on a 737. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N624UX (E175, left, 2026-08-28): the navy line was the mainline's path and sat 0.1-0.5 too high aft; on the E175 it runs just under both doors' sills and stays low (y about -0.45) under the tail, meeting the tail cone low down, so it's redrawn from this photo (heights read against the fuselage's outline in each column; within about 0.05). No measured E175 shape yet.",
  "history": "United Express jets have worn the 2019 scheme on delivery or repaint since 2019; the 2010 scheme (express-2010) is being painted out."
}
